{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1426 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "3b09b6fbff37ba8c1c235d0b00a79c28bd9c2d4af13f6dda031082f74c47529e" :edb/db-before-t 1425 :edb/db-after-t 1426 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534738 50 #inst "2026-10-08T05:32:46.016Z" 13194139534738 true] [17592186128770 1100 "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15} \\sum_{j=1}^{18} (a_{i} - 2)( b_{j}+1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15}a_i = 40, \\qquad \\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^{18}b_j =-8 .\n$$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186128770 1100 "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15} \\sum_{j=1}^{18} (a_{i} - 2)(b_{j}+1)$\n\ngiven that\n\n$\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15}a_i = 40, \\qquad \\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^{18}b_j =-8$." 13194139534738 false] [17592186128770 1145 "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n  a_{i}b_j = \\sum_{i=1}^m a_i \\sum_{j=1}^n b_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({b}_{j}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({b}_{j}+1) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}1) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}1) \\\\  & =(40-2\\cdot 15)\\cdot (-8+18) \\\\  & =(10)\\cdot (10) \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186128770 1145 "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n a_{i}b_j = \\sum_{i=1}^m a_i \\sum_{j=1}^n b_{j}\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(15)∑_(j = 1)^(18)(a_{i} - 2)(b_{j} + 1) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(15)(a_{i} - 2)∑_(j = 1)^(18)(b_{j} + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(15)(a_{i} - 2)∑_(j = 1)^(18)(b_{j} + 1) &= (∑_(i = 1)^(15)a_{i} - ∑_(i = 1)^(15)2) \\cdot (∑_(j = 1)^(18)b_{j} + ∑_(j = 1)^(18)1) \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(15)a_{i} - 2∑_(i = 1)^(15)1) \\cdot (∑_(j = 1)^(18)b_{j} + ∑_(j = 1)^(18)1) \\\\\n&= (40 - 2 \\cdot 15) \\cdot (-8 + 18) \\\\\n&= (10) \\cdot (10) \\\\\n&= 100\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534738 false] [17592186128927 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^3\\sum_{i=1}^2 (i+j)$." 13194139534738 false] [17592186128927 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^3\\sum_{i=1}^2 (i+j).$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186128927 1145 "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(j = 1)^(3)∑_(i = 1)^(2)(i + j) &= ∑_(j = 1)^(3)[∑_(i = 1)^(2)(i + j)] \\\\\n&= ∑_(j = 1)^(3)[(1 + j) + (2 + j)] \\\\\n&= ∑_(j = 1)^(3)(3 + 2j)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the sum above by summing over the index $j$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(j = 1)^(3)(3 + 2j) &= (3 + 2 \\cdot 1) + (3 + 2 \\cdot 2) + (3 + 2 \\cdot 3) \\\\\n&= 5 + 7 + 9 \\\\\n&= 21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534738 false] [17592186128927 1145 "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j) & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[(1+j)+(2+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the sum above by summing over the index $j\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j) & =(3+2\\cdot 1)+(3+2\\cdot 2)+(3+2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =5+7+9 \\\\  & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186128928 1100 "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8}  a_{ij} = 8, \\qquad\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8}  b_{ij} = 15.\n$$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186128928 1100 "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij})$\n\ngiven that\n\n$\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} a_{ij} = 8, \\qquad\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} b_{ij} = 15$." 13194139534738 false] [17592186128928 1145 "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(a_{ij} + b_{ij}) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)a_{ij} + ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)b_{ij}, \\\\\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)ka_{ij} &= k∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)a_{ij}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)(1 + 2a_{ij} - b_{ij}) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1 + ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)2a_{ij} - ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)b_{ij} \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 2∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)a_{ij} - ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)b_{ij} \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 2(8) - 15 \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n 1 = mn\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 1 &= 5 \\cdot 8 + 1 \\\\\n&= 40 + 1 \\\\\n&= 41\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij}) = 41\n$$" 13194139534738 false] [17592186128928 1145 "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}(1+2{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}2{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+2(8)-15 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n 1 = mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+1 & =5\\cdot 8+1 \\\\  & =40+1 \\\\  & =41.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij}) = 41.\n$$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186129108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306782 13194139534738 true] [17592186129108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306789 13194139534738 true] [17592186129108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306796 13194139534738 true] [17592186129108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306803 13194139534738 true] [17592186129109 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306719 13194139534738 true] [17592186129109 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306726 13194139534738 true] [17592186129109 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306733 13194139534738 true] [17592186129109 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306740 13194139534738 true] [17592186129194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306747 13194139534738 true] [17592186129194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306754 13194139534738 true] [17592186129194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306761 13194139534738 true] [17592186129194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306768 13194139534738 true] [17592186129194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306775 13194139534738 true] [17592186129435 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534738 true] [17592186129435 1100 "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nFind the value of the double sum\n\n$∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(10)(1 - a_{ij} - b_{ij})$\n\ngiven that\n\n$∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(10)a_{ij} = 10, ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(10)b_{ij} = 20$." 13194139534738 false] [17592186129435 1100 "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1-{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}=10,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij}=20.\n$$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186129435 1145 "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1-{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)-10-20 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)-30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)-30 & =5\\cdot 10-30 \\\\  & =50-30 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1-{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})=20.\n$$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186129787 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534738 true] [17592186129787 1100 "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij=$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186129787 1100 "What is $∑_(j = 1)^(2)∑_(i = 1)^(3)ij$?" 13194139534738 false] [17592186129787 1145 "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(1j+2j+3j) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(j+2j+3j) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}6j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}6j & =6\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6+12 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186306719 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306720 13194139534738 true] [17592186306719 1089 "q-149656" 13194139534738 true] [17592186306719 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534738 true] [17592186306719 1100 "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}5({a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{a}_{ij}=220,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{b}_{ij}=200.\n$$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186306719 1113 #uuid "38d56462-cbf1-5e86-b460-023450c63c10" 13194139534738 true] [17592186306719 1145 "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}5({a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & =5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}({a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) \\\\  & =5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{a}_{ij}-5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 220-5\\cdot 200 \\\\  & =1,100-1,000 \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534738 true] [17592186306720 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306721 13194139534738 true] [17592186306720 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306722 13194139534738 true] [17592186306720 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306723 13194139534738 true] [17592186306720 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306724 13194139534738 true] [17592186306720 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306725 13194139534738 true] [17592186306720 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534738 true] [17592186306720 1041 "selection" 13194139534738 true] [17592186306720 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306724 13194139534738 true] [17592186306720 1110 #uuid "3f37c383-59c0-59e7-ba25-a8e19ba845d3" 13194139534738 true] [17592186306721 1034 "130